# The foes' plans through the editor's agent pane (#13466, #13465), for coax drive
# (docs/editor/acceptance/README.md, "Foes in the agent pane"). Start from an empty world on the dev
# server. Size 1600x900, query "edit=agent", --real-time (#13475). Coder's local side is scripted: each
# /local/ route the page asks is answered from docs/editor/acceptance/foes-pane/, a Claude Code turn on
# Haiku 5.5 as it ran on a dev server. The edit verbs stand in for the agent's realm tools: each fails
# the run unless the world takes it and the open editor stands at its revision.
answer /local/sessions docs/editor/acceptance/foes-pane/sessions.json
answer /local/claude docs/editor/acceptance/foes-pane/claude.json
answer /local/agents docs/editor/acceptance/foes-pane/agents.json
answer /local/run docs/editor/acceptance/foes-pane/run.txt
answer /local/log docs/editor/acceptance/foes-pane/log.jsonl
clock +12000
# the world the note names: the page's own revision, read from this server
state page.f.rev
# the agent menu: Claude Code, which starts on Haiku 5.5
tap agent=OpenAgents
clock +500
tap agent=Claude Code
clock +1000
type composer At dawn the Imperial robots sweep the village gate in pairs and the raiders sleep by the fire. At dusk the raiders circle the party mine and two robots stand guard at the tunnel mouth. Then set the editor's time to dusk so I can watch.
type composer key Enter
clock +3000
screenshot apps/openagents-web/build/foes-pane-turn.png
# what the agent's tools write, arriving in the open editor one revision at a time
plan 6 dusk guard
route 6 dusk -200 -3700, 0 -3100
plan 7 dusk guard
route 7 dusk 200 -3700, 0 -3100
plan 1 dusk patrol
route 1 dusk 150 -3100, 0 -1900, -150 -3100, 0 -4300
time dusk
clock +1000
state page.f.rev
state game.view
screenshot apps/openagents-web/build/foes-pane-dusk.png
# put the world back: seven edits, then the story's own clock
undo
undo
undo
undo
undo
undo
undo
state page.f.rev
logs
